<DocsLayout
  title="aegis test"
  description="Execute generated security tests against an existing analysis."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: "CLI reference", href: "/docs/cli/" }, { label: "test" }]}
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="name">NAME</h2>
  <p><code>aegis test</code> — run the verification step on its own.</p>

  <h2 id="synopsis">SYNOPSIS</h2>
  <CodeBlock title="synopsis">aegis test [FINDING_ID ...]
    [--target=URL] [--command=COMMAND] [--timeout=DURATION]
    [--keep-artifacts] [--dry-run] [GLOBAL_FLAGS ...]</CodeBlock>

  <h2 id="description">DESCRIPTION</h2>
  <p>
    <code>aegis test</code> reuses the analysis stored in
    <code>.aegis/</code> by the last scan and runs its generated tests
    again. Use it to re-verify a finding after a fix, or to run verification in
    an environment where the service is available but the source is not.
  </p>
  <p>
    Without arguments, every candidate from the last analysis is tested. With
    one or more <code>FINDING_ID</code> arguments, only those are tested.
  </p>

  <h2 id="examples">EXAMPLES</h2>
  <CodeBlock title="shell"># Re-verify everything from the last scan
aegis test

# Re-verify one finding after a fix
aegis test sql-injection-1

# Test a deployed instance instead of a locally started one
aegis test --target https://staging.example.com

# Show the generated tests without running them
aegis test --dry-run</CodeBlock>

  <h2 id="flags">FLAGS</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>[FINDING_ID ...]</dt>
    <dd>Findings to verify. Identifiers appear in the scan output and in JSON results.</dd>
    <dt>--target=URL</dt>
    <dd>Run tests against a running instance instead of starting one locally.</dd>
    <dt>--command=COMMAND</dt>
    <dd>Command used to start the application under test. Overrides <code>tests.command</code>.</dd>
    <dt>--timeout=DURATION</dt>
    <dd>Per-test timeout. Default is <code>90s</code>.</dd>
    <dt>--keep-artifacts</dt>
    <dd>Preserve requests, responses, and logs under <code>.aegis/artifacts/</code>.</dd>
    <dt>--dry-run</dt>
    <dd>Print the tests that would run, then exit without executing them.</dd>
  </dl>

  <h2 id="exit-status">EXIT STATUS</h2>
  <p>
    <code>0</code> when no test reproduced a finding at or above
    <code>report.fail_on</code>, <code>1</code> when one did, <code>4</code>
    when the application under test could not be started.
  </p>

  <h2 id="see-also">SEE ALSO</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/docs/cli/scan/">aegis scan</a>,
    <a href="/docs/cli/report/">aegis report</a>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
